{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-associative_aggregation-java-generation-01","problem":"Implement `Solution.java` with a public final class `Solution` exposing exactly this API:

`public static Map<String, String> summarizeInspections(String[] records)`

Each non-null record is intended to have exactly four semicolon-separated fields:

`vehicleId;damaged;destroyed;operational`

A record is valid only when `vehicleId` is non-empty and each of the final three fields is exactly `true` or `false` in lowercase. Ignore malformed records, including records with missing or extra fields, invalid boolean text, an empty vehicle ID, or a null entry. If `records` is null, return an empty map.

Group valid records by vehicle ID. For each vehicle, the returned value must be `D,X,O`, where `D` is the number of its records with `damaged=true`, `X` is the number with `destroyed=true`, and `O` is the number with `operational=true`. Map iteration order is unspecified.

Use only the Java standard library. The implementation must not access the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks.","reference_code":"import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {
    }

    public static Map<String, String> summarizeInspections(String[] records) {
        Map<String, int[]> totals = new HashMap<>();
        if (records == null) {
            return new HashMap<>();
        }

        for (String record : records) {
            if (record == null) {
                continue;
            }
            String[] fields = record.split(";", -1);
            if (fields.length != 4 || fields[0].isEmpty()
                    || !isBoolean(fields[1])
                    || !isBoolean(fields[2])
                    || !isBoolean(fields[3])) {
                continue;
            }

            int[] counts = totals.computeIfAbsent(fields[0], key -> new int[3]);
            if (fields[1].equals("true")) {
                counts[0]++;
            }
            if (fields[2].equals("true")) {
                counts[1]++;
            }
            if (fields[3].equals("true")) {
                counts[2]++;
            }
        }

        Map<String, String> result = new HashMap<>();
        for (Map.Entry<String, int[]> entry : totals.entrySet()) {
            int[] counts = entry.getValue();
            result.put(entry.getKey(), counts[0] + "," + counts[1] + "," + counts[2]);
        }
        return result;
    }

    private static boolean isBoolean(String value) {
        return value.equals("true") || value.equals("false");
    }
}
