","known_bad_label":"Malformed boolean fields are accepted as valid records instead of being ignored."},{"id":"cap-v2-associative_aggregation-java-generation-02","problem":"Implement `Solution.java` with a public final class `Solution` exposing exactly this API:

`public static Map<String, Integer> sumAcceptedUnits(String[] lines)`

Each non-null line is intended to contain exactly three pipe-separated fields:

`itemCode|locationCode|units`

A line is valid only if both codes are non-empty strings containing exclusively uppercase ASCII letters and digits, and `units` is a base-10 integer from 1 through 100000 inclusive. Ignore malformed lines, including invalid field counts, invalid codes, non-integer quantities, out-of-range quantities, and null entries. If `lines` is null, return an empty map.

For every location appearing in a valid line, return the sum of units across all valid lines for that location. The caller guarantees that each resulting sum fits in an `int`. Map iteration order is unspecified.

Use only the Java standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks.","reference_code":"import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {
    }

    public static Map<String, Integer> sumAcceptedUnits(String[] lines) {
        Map<String, Integer> totals = new HashMap<>();
        if (lines == null) {
            return totals;
        }

        for (String line : lines) {
            if (line == null) {
                continue;
            }
            String[] fields = line.split("\\|", -1);
            if (fields.length != 3 || !isCode(fields[0]) || !isCode(fields[1])) {
                continue;
            }

            final int units;
            try {
                units = Integer.parseInt(fields[2]);
            } catch (NumberFormatException exception) {
                continue;
            }
            if (units < 1 || units > 100000) {
                continue;
            }

            totals.merge(fields[1], units, Integer::sum);
        }
        return totals;
    }

    private static boolean isCode(String value) {
        if (value.isEmpty()) {
            return false;
        }
        for (int i = 0; i < value.length(); i++) {
            char character = value.charAt(i);
            boolean letter = character >= 'A' && character <= 'Z';
            boolean digit = character >= '0' && character <= '9';
            if (!letter && !digit) {
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
