","known_bad_label":"A TreeMap emits routes in lexicographic order instead of the supplied route order."},{"id":"cap-v2-binary_and_bitwise-java-generation-01","problem":"Implement `Solution.java` with a public final class `Solution` exposing exactly this API:

`public static int[] decodeReadings(byte[] packed)`

The input length is guaranteed to be even. Each consecutive pair of bytes encodes one sensor reading. In the first byte, bits 7 through 5 contain an unsigned sensor ID from 0 through 7, while bits 4 through 0 contain the upper five bits of an unsigned 13-bit reading. The second byte contains the lower eight bits of that reading.

Return an array containing two integers per encoded pair: the sensor ID followed by the decoded reading. Interpret all bytes as unsigned bit patterns.

Every invocation must be state-isolated: allocate and return a fresh result array, retain no input or result array in mutable static state, and do not modify `packed`. Consequently, later calls or caller mutations of arrays from one call must not affect results from another call.

Use only the Java standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks.","reference_code":"public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {
    }

    public static int[] decodeReadings(byte[] packed) {
        int readingCount = packed.length / 2;
        int[] result = new int[readingCount * 2];

        for (int readingIndex = 0; readingIndex < readingCount; readingIndex++) {
            int header = packed[readingIndex * 2] & 0xFF;
            int lowByte = packed[readingIndex * 2 + 1] & 0xFF;
            int sensorId = (header >>> 5) & 0x07;
            int reading = ((header & 0x1F) << 8) | lowByte;

            result[readingIndex * 2] = sensorId;
            result[readingIndex * 2 + 1] = reading;
        }
        return result;
    }
}
","known_bad_code":"public final class Solution {
    private static int[] scratch = new int[0];

    private Solution() {
    }

    public static int[] decodeReadings(byte[] packed) {
        int readingCount = packed.length / 2;
        if (scratch.length != readingCount * 2) {
            scratch = new int[readingCount * 2];
        }

        for (int readingIndex = 0; readingIndex < readingCount; readingIndex++) {
            int header = packed[readingIndex * 2] & 0xFF;
            int lowByte = packed[readingIndex * 2 + 1] & 0xFF;
            int sensorId = (header >>> 5) & 0x07;
            int reading = ((header & 0x1F) << 8) | lowByte;

            scratch[readingIndex * 2] = sensorId;
            scratch[readingIndex * 2 + 1] = reading;
        }
        return scratch;
    }
}
","known_bad_label":"The mutable static scratch array is reused across calls, so returned results are not state-isolated."}]}

